<title>JAPAN: Matsushita Elec Works to buy back 50 mln shares.</title>
<headline>Matsushita Elec Works to buy back 50 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Matsushita Electric Works Ltd said on Monday it has decided to buy back 50 million of its shares.</p>
<p>The company, a leading maker of building materials and lighting equipment, plans to spend 50 billion yen to buy the shares from the market in the year following a shareholder's meeting planned for February 27, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>It had issued a total of 774 million shares as of the end of November. Matsushita Electric Works is a group company of Japanese electronics giant Matsushita Electric Industrial Co Ltd.</p>
</text>
